node_modules/
*.tgz

# `lib/` is deliberately NOT ignored here.
#
# `main` and `exports` point into it, and a git dependency is packed from the
# repository, not from the machine that built it. With `lib/` ignored, a git
# install (`dsh plugin add github:argszero/cordis-plugin-tool-deadline-guard#<tag>`)
# exits 0 and leaves a package whose entry point does not exist: installation
# succeeds, mounting cannot.
#
# The npm tarball was never affected — `prepublishOnly` runs `tsc` before packing
# — which is exactly why this went unnoticed: the channel that works hid the one
# that does not. `test/packaging.spec.mjs` now asserts both halves of the
# contract, so removing the build output from the repository fails the suite.
